# Handoff

Authoritative standard: `.ai/MASTER_WORKFLOW.md`, `.ai/HANDOFF_TEMPLATE.md`, and
`docs/agent/CLOUD_HANDOFF.md`.

## Private operational handoffs (gitignored)

- Regenerate root `HANDOFF.md` and `CHANGELOG_SESSION.md` after success, failure, blocker,
  partial completion, review requirement, context exhaustion, quota interruption, credential
  failure, or environment failure.
- Statuses only: `IN_PROGRESS`, `REVIEW_REQUIRED`, `BLOCKED`, `FAILED`, `READY`. Never `DRAFT`.
- `CHANGELOG_SESSION.md` is the current session only, not an infinite log.
- Compute `Source File SHA256` with `grep -v '^Source File SHA256:' <file> | shasum -a 256`.
- Do not stage these files into commits. On Local Mac, run
  `~/.local/bin/sync-aidataengineer-handoff.sh` and verify SHA256 + `cmp`.

## Tracked run reports (committed)

- Every agent run on a task branch must create exactly one report at
  `docs/agent/runs/<TASK_ID>/<SESSION_ID>.md` (never overwrite).
- Run-report statuses only: `SUCCESS`, `PARTIAL`, `BLOCKED`, `FAILED`, `REVIEW_REQUIRED`.
- Cloud agents: run report is mandatory before push; private handoffs must not be staged.
- Parallel agents: distinct task ID, branch, session ID, run report, file ownership, base/final
  commit, dependencies, and integration order when relevant.
- Never include secrets, tokens, passwords, private keys, or sensitive environment values.
